NOTICE
======

This project builds on several remarkable open-source projects:

- PocketTTS (Kyutai) — text-to-speech
  https://github.com/kyutai/pocket-tts
- sherpa-onnx (k2-fsa) — speech recognition runtime
  https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
- Parakeet TDT CTC 110M (NVIDIA) — ASR weights
  https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt_ctc-110m
- yt-dlp — video download
  https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
- FFmpeg — audio/video pipeline
  https://ffmpeg.org/
- FastAPI + Uvicorn — HTTP service
  https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/

Design lineage: a much-opinionated evolution of ideas sketched in
  https://github.com/davidtkunz/movie-sign
Which shows what happens when you let MST3K watch any movie. This project
takes that basic observation and runs it through a real comedy pipeline —
contextual transcript awareness, per-shot bundles, two-voice chemistry —
so the riffs land like they were written by someone watching the movie.

Voices are shipped as pre-built PocketTTS presets; each preset was bundled
by the upstream PocketTTS project from public-domain LibriVox narration.
The theater overlay is procedural / original, no copyrighted assets used.
